These fixtures and checks cover the libsndfile-backed W64 and CAF float paths.

The four fixture files were written by the unmodified SoX tree at 8 kHz, mono,
with a 1 kHz sine wave at -20 dBFS. The f32 files contain normalized floating
point samples. The f64 files contain the integer-scale double representation
written by the existing SoX libsndfile path.

The test verifies:

1. Pre-fix f32 W64 and CAF files read at their stored level.
2. Pre-fix f64 W64 and CAF files retain their established read behavior.
3. Current f32 and f64 W64 and CAF write/read round trips retain level.

The f64 checks prevent an f32 repair from changing the existing double path
without also solving its separate read and write compatibility problem.
